    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="1049" n="935" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg935"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.4016/610</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geddes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your communication of
                    the 14th instant in regard to the proposed investigation in Asia Minor by
                    Commissions to be selected by the International Red Cross, I take pleasure in
                    informing you that the American Legation at Berne has been authorized to advance
                    to the International Red Cross the equivalent of £1,000 which this Government
                    has agreed to contribute toward the expenses of the Commissions.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
